-- title:
--   Two minimal primes of (q) in the finite-j chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0\ge 1$, let $q$ be a prime with $q\nmid N_0$, and write $F=\,$`modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N_0q$. Let $W:\mathrm{Fin}\,2\to$ valuation subrings of $F$ satisfy: (i) $f\in W_0$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo $q$ (coefficientwise, via $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Z}/q$) and $f\cdot y=x$ after coefficientwise base change to $\mathbb{Q}$; (ii) $f\in W_1$ if and only if `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N₀ q` applied to $f$ lies in $W_0$, where that map is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ with the property `IsAtkinLehnerAutFull N₀ q` when one exists and the identity otherwise; (iii) $W_0\ne W_1$; (iv) for each $i$, the image of $q$ is a nonunit of $W_i$, for every $P\in\mathbb{Z}[X]$ with nonzero reduction modulo $q$ both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $W_i$ (here $j$ is the element `jq` of $F$), and every nonunit $f$ of $W_i$ satisfies $fq^{-1}\in W_i$; (v) conversely, any valuation subring $V$ of $F$ in which $q$ is a nonunit and which contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for all such $P$ equals $W_0$ or $W_1$. Then there is a pair of ideals $P_0,P_1$ of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$-subalgebra $A=\,$`IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` of $F$ such that, for each $i$, an element of $A$ lies in $P_i$ exactly when its image in $F$ is a nonunit of $W_i$; each $P_i$ is prime; $P_0\ne P_1$; and the minimal primes of the ideal of $A$ generated by $q$ are precisely $P_0$ and $P_1$.
--
--   The statement identifies the generic points of the two components of the fibre at $q$ of the finite-$j$ chart of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$: the two minimal primes of $(q)$ in the chart ring are the centres of the Gauss valuation ring of the $\mathfrak q$-expansion at infinity and of its Atkin–Lehner transform. It feeds the analysis of the package-level model at $N_0q$, and is used in the study of the sections at the cusps and of the unramified quotients of the chart ring along the fibre.
